<<<
retro-. In most words the usual pronunciation is rétro; but in the commonest of all, retrospect & retrograde, it is rétro; in words derived from or allied with these two (reirospective, retrospection, retrogression, retrogressive, retrogradation) it varies,
===
**retro-.** In most words the usual pronunciation is rētro; but in the commonest of all, *retrospect & retrograde*, it is rĕtro; in words derived from or allied with these two *(retrospective, retrospection, retrogression, retrogressive, retrogradation)* it varies,
>>>

<<<
the tendency being to say rétro if the stress is shifted, as it is by most speakers in all these words, & by all in retrogradation, to the third or fourth syllable.
===
the tendency being to say rētro if the stress is shifted, as it is by most speakers in all these words, & by all in *retrogradation*, to the third or fourth syllable.
>>>

<<<
retrograd-, retrogress(-). There are two series: (1) adj. & vb retrograde, n. retrogradation; (2) vb retrogress, n. retrogression, adj. retrogresstwe.
===
**retrograd-, retrogress(-).** There are two series: (1) adj. & vb *retrograde*, n. *retrogradation*; (2) vb *retrogress*, n. *retrogression*, adj. *retrogressive*.
>>>
